---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 5, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Service | AlisPro MediTours"
	description="The terms governing your use of alispromeditours.com and AlisPro MediTours' medical tourism facilitation services."
>
	<PageHeader title="Terms of Service" subtitle={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated}`} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Terms of Service' }]} />

	<section class="legal-page">
		<div class="legal-page__inner">
			<p>
				These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of alispromeditours.com (the "Site") and the medical
				tourism facilitation services provided by AlisPro MediTours ("we", "us", "our"). By using the Site or
				engaging our services, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
			</p>

			<h2>1. What We Are — and What We Are Not</h2>
			<p>
				AlisPro MediTours is a medical tourism <strong>facilitation and coordination service</strong>. We help
				international patients connect with independent, third-party hospitals, clinics, and doctors in India, and
				coordinate related logistics such as travel and accommodation.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>We are not a hospital, clinic, medical practice, or insurer, and we do not practice medicine.</strong>{' '}
				We do not diagnose, treat, or provide medical advice. All diagnosis, treatment recommendations, and
				clinical decisions are made solely by the independent, licensed hospitals and doctors you are referred
				to, based on their own professional judgment.
			</p>

			<h2>2. Cost Estimates and Treatment Information</h2>
			<p>
				Costs, savings percentages, treatment durations, hospital stay lengths, and similar figures shown on the
				Site are <strong>indicative estimates only</strong>, based on typical cases and information available to
				us at the time. They are not quotes, do not account for every individual's medical complexity, and are
				subject to change once a hospital reviews your specific reports. Final pricing, treatment plans, and
				timelines are determined solely by the treating hospital.
			</p>

			<h2>3. No Guarantee of Outcomes</h2>
			<p>
				We make no representation or warranty, express or implied, regarding the outcome of any medical
				procedure, the availability of any doctor or hospital, visa approval, or travel arrangements. Medical
				treatment carries inherent risks that exist regardless of where or by whom it is performed, and we are
				not liable for any medical outcome, complication, misdiagnosis, malpractice, or other act or omission of
				any third-party hospital, doctor, or other provider.
			</p>

			<h2>4. Your Responsibilities</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Provide accurate, complete, and up-to-date medical, personal, and travel information.</li>
				<li>Obtain any visas, travel documents, or legal clearances required for international travel.</li>
				<li>Make your own informed decision about any treatment, after discussing it directly with the treating doctor.</li>
				<li>Comply with the policies of any hospital, hotel, airline, or other third party you engage with through our coordination.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>5. Fees</h2>
			<p>
				Any coordination or service fees charged by AlisPro MediTours, separate from hospital or third-party
				charges, will be disclosed to you before you commit to engaging our services. Hospital, doctor, travel,
				and accommodation charges are set independently by those third parties and are not controlled by us.
			</p>

			<h2>6. Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
			<p>
				The Site may reference or link to third-party hospitals, hotels, airlines, insurers, or other services.
				We are not responsible for the content, accuracy, availability, or practices of any third-party service,
				and your use of them is governed by their own terms and policies.
			</p>

			<h2>7. Intellectual Property</h2>
			<p>
				All text, graphics, logos, and other content on the Site, except third-party content, is owned by or
				licensed to AlisPro MediTours and may not be copied, reproduced, or distributed without our prior written
				permission.
			</p>

			<h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
			<p>
				To the fullest extent permitted by law, AlisPro MediTours shall not be liable for any indirect,
				incidental, special, or consequential damages, or any loss of data, revenue, or profits, arising from
				your use of the Site or our facilitation services, including but not limited to any medical outcome or
				act or omission of a third-party provider.
			</p>

			<h2>9. Indemnification</h2>
			<p>
				You agree to indemnify and hold AlisPro MediTours harmless from any claim, loss, or damage arising from
				your breach of these Terms, your misuse of the Site, or your interactions with third-party hospitals,
				doctors, or service providers.
			</p>

			<h2>10. Governing Law</h2>
			<p>
				These Terms are governed by the laws of India, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute
				arising under these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of New Delhi,
				India.
			</p>

			<h2>11. Changes to These Terms</h2>
			<p>
				We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by updating the "Last
				updated" date above. Continued use of the Site after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the
				revised Terms.
			</p>

			<h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about these Terms can be sent to{' '}
				<a href="mailto:care@alispromeditours.com">care@alispromeditours.com</a> or 238 Westend Mall, Janakpuri,
				New Delhi, Delhi 110058, India.
			</p>

			<p class="legal-page__disclaimer">
				This document is provided for general informational purposes and does not constitute legal advice. It
				should be reviewed by a qualified attorney — particularly regarding medical-disclaimer language and
				liability limitations relevant to your jurisdiction — before being relied upon as a complete, enforceable
				agreement.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.legal-page {
		background: var(--color-bg-white);
		padding: 56px 24px 88px;
		font-family: var(--font-body);
	}

	.legal-page__inner {
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.legal-page__inner p {
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		margin: 0 0 18px;
	}

	.legal-page__inner ul {
		margin: 0 0 18px;
		padding-left: 22px;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
	}

	.legal-page__inner li {
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.75;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}

	.legal-page__inner h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 20px;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--color-text-primary);
		margin: 36px 0 14px;
	}

	.legal-page__inner a {
		color: var(--color-primary);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.legal-page__disclaimer {
		margin-top: 40px;
		padding-top: 20px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);
		font-size: 13px;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		font-style: italic;
	}
</style>
